o you think the  prosecution dismissed this case why not  leave it to a potential jury to decide  according to the prosecutor there was  exculpatory evidence  that the sheriff wasn't aware of and  that this made it less likely for him to  be able to get a conviction and that's  the most important thing here  prosecutors don't want to bring a case  unless they think they can get a  conviction even though sometimes there  is evidence if it has to rise the level  of beyond a reasonable doubt it's a very  high standard so if indeed there was  anything exculpatory that they did have  it makes sense that they decided hey  it's up to us to bring this not the  sheriff it never they may never have  brought it to begin with in this respect  it looks like maybe something's fishy  happening but if they had never brought  up we never would be having this  conversation absolutely and and to add  to that point too prosecutors unlike  defense attorneys or other lawyers have  a very unique ethical duty to only  prosecute cases in which they think they  can win on they can't just bring  frivolous claims so to speak so thank  you for that both when we come back  emotional testimony from the defendant's  ex-girlfriend we head to wisconsin and  chandler-halterson stands trial for the  murder of his parents  welcome back to law and crime daily as  the first week of wisconsin vs chandler  haldison winds down the jury hears a  police interrogation with a defendant  for the first time  prosecutors say 23 year old chandler  hall in a senate murdered his parents 50  year old bart and 53 year old krista  halderson in july 2021 after that they  say halterson cut up their bodies and  attempted to burn their remains in the  family fireplace he laid or scattered  other body parts of theirs across  southern wisconsin on thursday  hardison's former girlfriend catherine  cat mildred meldrum  took the stand she told jurors holderson  asked her to bring ice hydrogen peroxide  and a swiffer wetjet to hi